3.3 Autoencoders
Embedding is performed with autoencoders. An autoencoder couples an encoder E and a decoder Dec: the encoder maps a modality input xm to a latent code zm = Em(xm), and the decoder reconstructs the input from that code, the pair being trained to minimize reconstruction error. One autoencoder is trained per modality, so that each latent-space is adapted to the statistics of its modality. The encoder architecture is chosen according to the data type of each modality; the specific choices used in this study are given in Section 4.
3.4 Generative Augmentation and Model Selection
Synthetic samples are produced with generative adversarial networks. A GAN couples a generator G, which maps a noise vector z ~ pz to a synthetic sample G(z), and a discriminator D, which learns to separate real samples x ~ pdata from synthetic


