Data acquisition comprised three primary modalities recorded for each participant:
● Time-series movement data: each subject completed 11 standardized motor tasks (e.g., finger taps, hand flips), lasting 1020 seconds, using two wrist-mounted Apple Watch Series 4 devices recording accelerometer (g) and gyroscope (rad/s) data at 100 Hz across three axes. Motion time-series were divided into uniform 10.24-second intervals, yielding 2^10 = 1024 samples per subject for FFT-based spectral analysis.
● PDNMS (Parkinson's Disease NonMotor Symptoms): a patient-reported


